            <ArticleTitle>Spontaneous bilateral chylothorax: uniform features of a rare condition.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>872-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 67-yr-old woman was admitted with dyspnoea, chest and neck pain and swelling of both supraclavicular fossae and the neck. Chest X-ray showed bilateral pleural effusions. Thoracocentesis yielded a milky fluid with a high triglyceride level. Four previously published cases had similar clinical manifestations. The pathophysiology is discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
